[285.481851, "o", ": status: approved\r\n205: \r\n206: ## Investigation Brief 02\r\n207: — Status Precedence\r\n208: \r\n209: Interview notes with the compliance desk confirmed status fights between mail,\r\n210: amendments, and corrections. Ledger rows provide the base status (lowercase on\r\n211: output). Status precedence from lowest to highest is: pending, approved,\r\n212: rejected, reversed. Email excerpts may change status only when the From line\r\n213: contains `compliance@` anywhere in the address; ignore all other senders.\r\n214: \r\n215: ## Investigation Brief 02\r\n216: — Status Precedence — supporting chronology\r\n217: \r\n218: Regional lead E. Novak hosted a readout on capital project capitalization where finance controllers disputed whether unsigned meeting notes should override ledger owners; investigators cited Brief 05 during the session.\r\n219: \r\n220: Site visit #525 to fixed assets exported 19 compliance threads tied to capital project capitalization. Reviewers noted that owner field churn appeared whenever correction batches s"]
[285.481936, "o", "traddled a weekend wire cutoff.\r\n221: \r\n\r\ncontext around 211\r\n208: \r\n209: Interview notes with the compliance desk confirmed status fights between mail,\r\n"]
[285.484375, "o", "210: amendments, and corrections. Ledger rows provide the base status (lowercase on\r\n211: output). Status precedence from lowest to highest is: pending, approved,\r\n212: rejected, reversed. Email excerpts may change status only when the From line\r\n213: contains `compliance@` anywhere in the address; ignore all other senders.\r\n214: \r\n215: ## Investigation Brief 02\r\n"]
[285.484461, "o", "216: — Status Precedence — supporting chronology\r\n217: \r\n218: Regional lead E. Novak hosted a readout on capital project capitalization where finance controllers disputed whether unsigned meeting notes should override ledger owners; investigators cited Brief 05 during the session.\r\n219: \r\n220: Site visit #525 to fixed assets exported 19 compliance threads tied to capital project capitalization. Reviewers noted that owner field churn appeared whenever correction batches straddled a weekend wire cutoff.\r\n221: \r\n222: Grant compliance WP-9559 tied capital project capitalization attestation gaps to ledger slice confusion visible only when hold flags used corrected rather than pre-correction ledger dates.\r\n223: \r\n224: Peer review #804 of fixed assets sampling found 19 mislinked emails on capital project capitalization. None of the mislinked messages originated from compliance addresses, supporting Brief 02 sender restrictions.\r\n225: \r\n"]
