[344.166813, "o", "agreed while noting those memos still inform exception coding narratives.\r\n703: \r\n704: Audit technologist R. Okonkwo replayed FY24 mailbox snapshots and showed how SOX sampling mismatch threads arrived out of order relative to correction notices, surfacing correction batch ordering on four high-balance rows.\r\n705: \r\n706: External advisors reviewing SOX sampling mismatch during March walkthrough asked for a machine-readable trace explaining why rejected rows received hold flags. The archive preserves narrative chronology even though only structured tail sections are authoritative.\r\n707: \r\n708: Peer review #521 of internal audit sampling found 17 mislinked emails on SOX sampling mismatch. None of the mislinked messages originated from compliance addresses, supporting Brief 02 sender restrictions.\r\n709: \r\n710: Site visit #842 to internal audit exported 22 compliance threads tied to SOX sampling mismatch. Reviewers noted that status precedence inversion appeared whenever correction batches straddled a weekend wir"]
